BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (Every practitioner opens with the same number. Drawback refunds 99% of eligible duties, taxes and fees,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (and in Monica Pascarella's words it is only 99% because 1% is kept in customs for administrative fees) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm ([1_L7fnmAAU0 @ 00:02:37]. The eligible bucket is consistent across brokers and counsel. Joe Harper of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (Star USA lists ordinary duty, Section 301, HMF, MPF, marking duties, IRS taxes and 201 duties. Harper also) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (flags that MPF minimums and maximums require special math [NK99CBNOeJA @ 00:06:34]. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (Scarbrough webinar team adds voluntary tender and prior disclosure duties to the list, and describes Section) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (301 recovery as getting 'that 25 percent back' [6Ogi9iKVSTE @ 00:19:43]. The exclusion list is just as) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (uniform: AD/CVD, Section 232 and over-quota agricultural duties do not come back. Aaron Mandelbaum of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (Thompson Hine extends the line into the newest tariffs. IEEPA reciprocal duties fall on the eligible side and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (IEEPA fentanyl tariffs on the ineligible side, while some 232 carve-outs are starting to emerge) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm ([WqGvMD-AOqg @ 00:11:23]. The operating consensus is blunt. Before modeling any refund, strip 232,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (AD/CVD and over-quota lines out of the duty base, because no claim structure recovers them. The 301,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm (201, MPF and HMF lines stay in the recoverable pool that the rest of the program is built around.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 518.07 Tm (Substitution is where the consensus sharpens into hard classification rules. Scarbrough Global describes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 502.85 Tm (the old 'commercially interchangeable' test, which weighed four factors: government or industry standards,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 487.62 Tm (part numbers, tariff classifications and relative value. They call it unwieldy and subjective, while the TFTEA) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 472.40 Tm (standard is a much more objective 8-digit HTS match [fI28fmPlbPA @ 00:01:39]. Their commingled-bin) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 457.17 Tm (customer illustrates the upside. That customer sources the same item from four countries plus a domestic) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 441.95 Tm (supplier and still substitutes, as long as it is not an other provision. The rule set repeats everywhere. If the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 426.72 Tm (8-digit line is an 'other' provision, drop to the 10-digit code, and if the 10-digit code is also 'other', substitution) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 411.50 Tm (is barred [6Ogi9iKVSTE @ 00:14:47]. Alliance Duty Drawback Services confirms that part numbers are) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 396.27 Tm (ignored under the HTS match. Substitution is barred for exports to Canada, Mexico, Chile and US territories.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 381.05 Tm (The lesser-of rule caps recovery, so a $100 import matched to a $50 export recovers half [mkogoOMopss @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 365.82 Tm (00:03:26]. Mandelbaum states the cap plainly: claimants are 'only getting refunded the smaller of the two) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 350.60 Tm (duty amounts which prevents over refunds when substituted goods are used' [WqGvMD-AOqg @ 00:27:58].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 335.37 Tm (Alliance's operator takeaway is to substitute exports of similar value so the cap does not eat the claim.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 320.15 Tm (The third point of agreement is the clock and the privilege structure built around it. Matt Robison of Amber) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 304.92 Tm (Road credits TFTEA 2015 with two changes. It brought 8-digit substitution, and it collapsed the old) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 289.70 Tm (3-years-to-export plus 3-years-to-file timeline into a single 5-year clock. Robison also credits ACE's fully) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 274.47 Tm (electronic filing, live in 2019, with replacing mailed PDFs [BCWMDlUCSx4 @ 00:08:19]. Pat Caulfield of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 259.25 Tm (Scarbrough explains how to use the one-time retroactive waiver. Operators should 'pick a day' for the Notice) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 244.02 Tm (of Intent first, or lose three to six months of claimable imports while paperwork drifts [wEYqdvTPaqM @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 228.80 Tm (00:32:45]. The Scarbrough webinar calls the look-back 'your one-time get out of jail free card that allows you) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 213.57 Tm (to look back five years', and sets the clock by the submission date [6Ogi9iKVSTE @ 00:09:10]. Tisha Paige) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 198.35 Tm (of CEDA operationalizes the same logic. CEDA files claims the same day the privilege application goes in,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 183.12 Tm (locking the 5-year window from each import date. It then waits 3 to 18 months for CBP approval and about) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 167.90 Tm (45 days per claim for payment [SO9sA-x5K0k @ 00:33:40]. ITM and CEDA both call drawback a privilege,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 152.67 Tm (not a right. Every month the submission slips, the oldest entries age out of the five-year window.) Tj ET
