BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 526.30 Tm (Recon cycle completed, before any drawback filing [6Ogi9iKVSTE @ 00:22:48]. Tisha Paige lists the full) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 511.07 Tm (packet for an unused-merchandise privilege application. The import side needs the commercial invoice,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 495.85 Tm (packing slip and 7501. The export side needs the invoice, packing slip and proof of export: a bill of lading,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 480.62 Tm (B3/CAD, pedimento, airway bill or seaway bill. Inventory receipt and withdrawal dates complete the packet,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 465.40 Tm (and a manufacturing application adds production in/out dates and the bill of materials [SO9sA-x5K0k @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 450.17 Tm (00:29:46]. CEDA accepts paper records and has flown staff to clients to collect them.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 434.95 Tm (Refund size is engineered through accounting method and matching logic, not just paperwork. Monica) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 419.72 Tm (Pascarella walks through six accounting methods: FIFO, LIFO, low-to-high, low-to-high average inventory) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 404.50 Tm (turnover, low-to-high blanket and average. Low-to-high blanket is the most common, but 'not always' the) Tj ET
